# Confirmed commit chain

- f6fc7ac: send admission calls per-id transition with tolerant history reads;
  malformed historical JSON lines do not globally veto a send.
- e7d81c7 (2026-10-20 17:50:14-05:00): begin_attempt replaces per-id writes
  with file-global _items(strict=True) before candidate batch validation.
  Incomplete historical records throw before any transport send. The plain
  RuntimeError initially escaped the poll and terminated CLI.
- 1b08402: typed WakeHistoryUnavailable is caught in pending poll and delivery
  held indefinitely; cursor/marker do not advance. This prevents the crash
  but preserves the delivery regression.
- 09017fb: get(_locked=True) becomes strict too, so transition/queued admission
  also encounters the global blocker, not only terminal send.
- 0f5014d and9d1666f: no changes to those admission files; installing/restarting
  those versions cannot repair this regression.

# Scope correction

The user wants new SSE auto-injection restored, not historic backlog archival.
Minimal candidate-scoped repair is being implemented; no quarantine, history
rewrite/delete, cursor reset or new generation architecture is in scope.
Recognized leading-NUL writer-shaped row identities remain tainted for that
request; they are not promoted to valid ownership. Independently valid new
candidates must not inherit an unrelated known damaged-id veto. Unbounded,
unknown, partial-read corruption remains a separate fail-closed case.

